WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:06.299
InGen's origins, Rexy's legacy, and an oddly
high number of reconciling couples.

00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:10.935
We're digging deep to unearth the finer points
of the entire "Jurassic Park" franchise.

00:00:10.935 --> 00:00:13.974
"How'd you do this?"

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.130
"I'll show you."

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:22.560
Sixty-five million years ago, the late Cretaceous
Period met the Paleogene Period.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.270
This marked the sudden mass extinction of
three-quarters of the animals and plants on

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.920
earth — including all dinosaurs.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.960
In a prologue for "Jurassic World: Dominion"
that was cut from the final version, viewers

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:38.220
are introduced to a host of dinosaurs like
the dreadnoughtus and Moros intrepidus — both

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.680
of which had been previously unseen in the
franchise.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:45.820
At the end of the prologue, the last dinosaur
to be introduced is the giganotosaurus, the

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:51.950
largest apex predator of all time, and it
quickly asserts its dominance over a Tyrannosaurus rex.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:55.520
This scene isn't only significant because
a genetically engineered version of the giganotosaurus

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.910
returns to reclaim that title later on in
the film, though.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.539
It also links back to the scene in the first
"Jurassic Park" film, when Alan, Ellie, and

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:08.759
Ian watch a short film about a mosquito getting
encased in amber and fossilized after drinking

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:10.018
the blood of a dinosaur.

00:01:10.018 --> 00:01:11.018
"Bingo!

00:01:11.018 --> 00:01:12.899
Dino DNA."

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.310
The prologue heavily suggests that it was
this mosquito — or rather, one like it — that

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:22.710
was later used by John Hammond and Sir Benjamin
Lockwood's company InGen to extract dinosaur

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:26.284
DNA and then create the T-rex in the 1980s.

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:31.869
By 1969, John Hammond had made his vested
interest in animals very clear, having opened

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:35.680
his first animal preserve, Animal Kingdom,
that year in Nairobi, Kenya.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:41.350
He also hires future Jurassic Park employee
Robert Muldoon to work there as the park warden.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.530
But taking care of and showcasing animals
already on the planet clearly isn't enough

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:49.990
for Hammond, and he soon sets out to bring
dinosaurs back into the modern world.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:53.770
Having dreamed up the idea of using the DNA
of creatures encased in amber — like the

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:58.350
mosquito — to clone extinct animals, he
starts working with a small research team,

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.700
calling his company the Hammond Foundation.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:05.680
In 1975, Hammond had secured enough investors
and a partnership with British entrepreneur

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.659
Sir Benjamin Lockwood.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:11.950
Together they found International Genetic
Technologies, a bio-engineering company more

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.310
commonly referred to as InGen.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:18.250
Working out of a laboratory in Lockwood's
basement, the pair teams up with scientists

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.640
and conducts research on bringing extinct
animals back to life.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.470
Here, they make plans for a dinosaur theme
park, which they name Jurassic Park.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:32.470
In 1982, InGen signs a 99-year-long lease
for Isla Sorna and the Muertes Archipelago

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:36.591
from the Costa Rican government, where they
plan to conduct research, and construction

00:02:36.591 --> 00:02:39.295
begins on Jurassic Park: San Diego.

00:02:39.295 --> 00:02:44.840
In 1984, almost a decade after founding InGen,
John Hammond and Sir Benjamin Lockwood have

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.670
their first major breakthrough.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:51.250
Still working out of Lockwood's estate, he,
Hammond, and their team of scientists begin

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:55.420
a fertilization test on an artificial ovum,
which is successful.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:00.480
A year later, they move their headquarters
to Palo Alto and successfully clone the prehistoric

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.040
DNA from the amber.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.810
But other changes are afoot at InGen, as Hammond
suspends construction on Jurassic Park: San

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:08.120
Diego indefinitely.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:12.730
Instead, he looks to move the park to Isla
Nublar in Costa Rica.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:16.870
InGen leases the island from the Costa Rican
government, adding it to the 99-year lease

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.480
they'd already agreed to.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.750
Now making use of the islands they leased,
InGen starts working on Isla Sorna, which

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:27.170
they call Site B — but they haven't been
able to clone a dinosaur yet, despite having

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.720
success with the amber.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.150
In 1986, Hammond and Lockwood add Dr. Henry
Wu to their team, and he suggests they splice

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.340
the DNA of dinosaurs with that of modern animals
like frogs.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:42.420
Shortly afterward, InGen successfully clones
their first dinosaur, a triceratops.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:47.000
Wu also comes up with the lysine contingency,
a plan that would theoretically protect the

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.520
humans if the dinosaurs ever escaped.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.160
By adding a faulty gene to the dinosaurs,
they'd become dependent on supplemental lysine

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.610
that InGen gave them.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:04:00.600
Removing dinosaurs from captivity, then, would
deprive them of the enriched food, send the

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.603
dinosaurs into a coma, and ultimately kill
them.

00:04:03.848 --> 00:04:09.340
Now seeing significant progress with its ability
to genetically engineer and replicate dinosaurs,

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:14.620
InGen goes ahead with plans for a new Jurassic
Park on Isla Nublar, which they refer to as

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:21.130
Site A. Construction begins on the island
in 1988 and is finished in 1993.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:25.790
During this period, InGen successfully hatches
more dinosaurs, including the Tyrannosaurus

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:30.600
rex "Rexy," who is seen throughout the "Jurassic
Park" and "Jurassic World" movies.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:36.370
Rexy is born on Site B but is moved over to
her paddock on Isla Nublar in 1989 when she's

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.509
one year old.

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:42.470
InGen has other innovative success thanks
to Dr. Henry Wu, who realizes that the DNA

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:47.600
of the yellow poison dart frog they've been
using is incompatible with some dinosaur genomes,

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.130
like velociraptors.

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:51.450
He suggests InGen uses the reed frog.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:56.289
Although any geneticist should suspect that
since the reed frog can change sex, this ability

00:04:56.289 --> 00:05:00.790
could be passed down to the dinosaurs, it's
ignored and is later the reason the dinosaurs

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:05.630
have been able to reproduce — a reveal seen
in "Jurassic Park" and expanded upon in "The

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.320
Lost World: Jurassic Park."

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.160
Wu also researches the hybridization of dinosaurs
during this period, which, of course, will

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.600
eventually lead to the Indominus Rex.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:19.530
However, InGen also suffers a major blow when
Sir Benjamin Lockwood leaves the company after

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:21.310
he and John Hammond fall out.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:25.340
Although the cause for this is not known in
"Jurassic Park", it's retconned into the story

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.030
in "Jurassic World: Dominion."

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:31.419
In this latest installment to the franchise,
we learn that Hammond was disgusted by Lockwood's

00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:35.949
interest in using their research for human
cloning after his daughter, Charlotte, who

00:05:35.949 --> 00:05:39.419
worked on Isla Sorna, revealed she wished
to have a baby this way.

00:05:39.419 --> 00:05:44.169
"Just like Blue, Charlotte was able to have
a child all by herself.

00:05:44.169 --> 00:05:47.765
She created you with her own DNA."

00:05:47.765 --> 00:05:52.540
Despite Sir Benjamin Lockwood's departure
from InGen, John Hammond forges ahead with

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:55.729
his plan to open Jurassic Park on Isla Nublar.

00:05:55.729 --> 00:05:59.480
However, the company's board of directors
has concerns about the park's safety after

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:04.470
gatekeeper Jophery Brown is killed by a Velociraptor
while transferring them to a higher security

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:07.400
holding pen and his family sues InGen.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:11.530
Nevertheless, Hammond believes Jurassic Park
is the perfect place to bring his grandchildren,

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.970
Lex and Tim, to get their minds off their
parents' divorce.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:20.160
Lawyer Donald Gennaro also heads to Isla Nublar
to assess the weaknesses of the park and whether

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:24.030
or not operations should be shut down before
the park even opens.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:27.669
He brings along Dr. Ian Malcolm for another
expert opinion.

00:06:27.669 --> 00:06:31.067
"Our scientists have done things which nobody
has ever done before."

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:35.260
"Yeah, but your scientists were so preoccupied
with whether or not they could but they didn't

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.680
stop to think if they should."

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:41.300
In response, Hammond invites Dr. Alan Grant
and Dr. Ellie Sattler along, hoping they will

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.350
endorse the park.

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:47.069
Elsewhere, Lewis Dodgson meets with Jurassic
Park computer programmer Dennis Nedry and

00:06:47.069 --> 00:06:53.386
convinces him to steal dinosaur embryos for
rival company BioSyn in exchange for $1.5 million.

00:06:53.386 --> 00:06:55.906
"The bottom screws open…

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.099
Its coolant is compartmentalized inside…"

00:07:01.376 --> 00:07:05.580
On June 11, everyone arrives at the park,
and the events of the first "Jurassic Park"

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.139
film take place over the next 48 hours.

00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:13.250
John Hammond takes Alan Grant, Ellie Sattler,
Ian Malcolm, and Donald Gennaro on a tour

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:18.250
of Jurassic Park where they see brachiosaurus
and parasaurolophus dinosaurs.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:23.706
The group is later joined by Lex and Tim,
but they see very few other dinosaurs that afternoon.

00:07:23.706 --> 00:07:28.230
An unexpected tropical storm heading toward
Isla Nublar then forces all non-essential

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:34.349
personnel to be evacuated, leaving only Nedry,
Hammond, Robert Muldoon, and Ray Arnold to

00:07:34.349 --> 00:07:36.100
manage the park.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:40.850
Nedry soon sneaks off to steal the embryos
and shuts down all power and security protocols

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:44.190
on the island, except for the velociraptor
holding pen.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:49.159
This allows Rexy to escape her paddock and
attack Lex, Tim, Ian and Alan.

00:07:49.159 --> 00:07:55.879
And Donald suffers one of the most memorable
deaths in cinema history.

00:07:55.879 --> 00:08:00.870
The same goes for Nedry, who doesn't quite
make it off the island with all of his stolen

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.530
embryos thanks to a run-in with a spunky dilophosaurus.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:09.140
In a bid to reverse Nedry's actions and get
the power back on, Ray does a full system

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:11.920
reset, but this deactivates the raptors' paddock.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:16.074
It's not long before Ray and Robert are both
devoured by the raptors.

00:08:17.779 --> 00:08:19.484
"Clever girl."

00:08:19.983 --> 00:08:26.669
This leaves Alan, Ellie, Ian, Hammond, Lex,
and Tim to get the power back on and call

00:08:26.669 --> 00:08:27.669
for help.

00:08:27.669 --> 00:08:31.919
They eventually do do this, but they encounter
the raptors several more times before being

00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:33.380
saved by Rexy.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:38.380
By the end of the film, even John concurs
Jurassic Park can't be saved, and the survivors

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.984
escape in a helicopter.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:43.899
"The Lost World: Jurassic Park" begins by
filling in the gaps of the past four years

00:08:43.899 --> 00:08:46.520
since InGen abandoned Isla Nublar.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.330
During this period, the bioengineering company
is hit with more lawsuits for the wrongful

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:55.351
deaths of Donald Gennaro, Robert Muldoon,
and Ray Arnold, which they covered up, and

00:08:55.351 --> 00:08:57.600
are nearly bankrupt because of it.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.820
Because of this, John Hammond is fired by
the board, and his nephew, Peter Ludlow, replaces

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:03.080
him as CEO.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:07.690
He makes plans to open Jurassic Park: San
Diego and wants to move over dinosaurs from

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:12.940
Site B. There are plenty because as Dr. Henry
Wu discovered, the lysine contingency had

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:16.790
proven ineffective and the remaining dinosaurs
began breeding.

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:21.840
Dr. Ian Malcolm breaks his non-disclosure
agreement with InGen to raise awareness over

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:26.310
the events on Isla Nublar, but is discredited
by Ludlow.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:30.329
Despite this, he initially refuses Hammond's
request for him to go to Site B with a small

00:09:30.329 --> 00:09:35.649
group of experts and document the dinosaurs
there and stop InGen from profiting off them.

00:09:35.649 --> 00:09:40.500
However, he changes his mind when his girlfriend,
Dr. Sarah Harding, is part of the group and

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:41.760
already on the island.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:46.570
He follows her there to "rescue" her but soon
discovers his teenage daughter Kelly has stowed

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.279
away on the rescue mission, too.

00:09:48.279 --> 00:09:52.400
Hammond's team, the "Gatherers," race against
InGen's "Hunters" but are ultimately forced

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:57.209
to work together after freed dinosaurs and
a pair of rexes destroy their vehicles and

00:09:57.209 --> 00:09:58.680
communication equipment.

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:04.089
After several encounters with the buck rex,
his female counterpart, and some velociraptors,

00:10:04.089 --> 00:10:09.510
the Gatherers escape the island, but Ludlow's
men capture the buck and take him to San Diego.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:14.170
Ian and Sarah use the young T. rex, "Junior,"
to lure him back onto the cargo ship.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:19.452
The ship sails back to Isla Sorna, but not
before Junior eats Ludlow.

00:10:19.452 --> 00:10:24.140
Following the events on Isla Sorna and in
San Diego, John Hammond petitions the government

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.610
to have Isla Sorna left as a nature reserve
for the dinosaurs.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:32.390
The U.S. House Committee of Science also passes
the Gene Guard Act, which gives bioengineered

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:36.070
dinosaurs the same status and rights as endangered
species.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:41.170
As a result, access to the islands is restricted
and InGen is forbidden from cloning any other

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.330
prehistoric flora or fauna.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.130
This seems to be the end of InGen's Jurassic
adventure.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:50.990
But when Hammond dies shortly after the events
of Lost World, Masrani Global swoops in and

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:53.410
acquires the bioengineering firm.

00:10:53.410 --> 00:10:59.029
Having taken over from his father as the CEO
of Masrani Global in 1992, Simon Masrani has

00:10:59.029 --> 00:11:02.200
kept a watchful eye over Hammond's company
for years.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:07.730
After taking over InGen in 1998, Masrani sets
out to fulfill Hammond's failed dream of opening

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:11.589
Jurassic Park, this time renamed Jurassic
World.

00:11:11.589 --> 00:11:16.089
Breaking the Gene Guard Act, he starts experimenting
mere months after Hammond's death.

00:11:16.089 --> 00:11:20.720
Shortly after, InGen begins secret experiments
on Site B with the goal of illegally breeding

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:24.750
new species, including the superpredator spinosaurus.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:30.000
Plans for a new park are underway, and in
1999, the U.N. grants Masrani Global legal

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.900
— but limited — access to Isla Sorna.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:37.730
Simon brings Dr. Henry Wu into his new "Jurassic
World" project in 2000 — who eventually

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.459
becomes the lead genetic biologist at InGen.

00:11:40.825 --> 00:11:44.950
"Jurassic Park III" begins by revealing what
Alan Grant and Ellie Sattler have been doing

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.610
in the eight years since they were on Isla
Nublar.

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:50.570
Notably, Ellie has retired from paleobotany.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:54.779
Although the two remain close, Ellie is now
married to Mark Degler, who works at the state

00:11:54.779 --> 00:11:57.290
department, and they have two young children
together.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:12:00.500
Meanwhile, Alan remains active in the field
of paleontology.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:04.210
In the beginning of the film, we see him and
his protégé, Billy Brennan, testing the

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:09.415
prototype of a machine that's able to craft
an accurate replica of a velociraptor voice box.

00:12:09.415 --> 00:12:15.916
"Wow…this is brilliant, Billy."

00:12:16.188 --> 00:12:21.850
It's here at this worksite that wealthy thrill-seeking
couple Paul and Amanda Kirby approach Alan

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:26.070
and offer to fund further research if he gives
them — and three mercenaries — an aerial

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:27.790
tour of Isla Nublar.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.339
Alan reluctantly agrees, and brings Billy
along with him.

00:12:31.339 --> 00:12:36.980
But the Kirbys' ulterior motive is soon revealed,
as the couple actually plans to rescue their

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:41.149
son, Eric, who — along with Amanda's boyfriend,
Ben Hildebrand — has gone missing on Isla

00:12:41.149 --> 00:12:44.930
Sorna after an illegal parasailing tour over
the island.

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:49.720
On the island, Alan finds Eric, now the sole
survivor, and reunites him with his parents.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:54.661
Their group faces attacks from velociraptors,
pteranodons, and the spinosaurus, and all

00:12:54.661 --> 00:12:57.320
three of the mercenaries are killed one by
one.

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:01.210
Alan gets out a distress call to Ellie and
Mark, though, who send a rescue team while

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.829
Alan fakes a distress call with his raptor
voice box to help them escape.

00:13:04.829 --> 00:13:08.984
Billy, believed to be dead, is later rescued
by the U.S. Marines.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:14.500
As a result of Alan and the Kirbys' actions
on Isla Sorna, a group of pteranodons escape

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.769
and are spotted over British Columbia.

00:13:16.769 --> 00:13:22.350
However, Simon Masrani hires security contractor
Vic Hoskins to deal with them; after doing

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:25.570
this, he is subsequently hired as InGen's
head of security.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:30.720
These events hadn't put Masrani off opening
his new park, Jurassic World, and in 2002

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:35.450
— a year after Alan's harrowing visit to
Isla Sorna — Masrani announces his plans

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.450
to the world.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:40.529
He also has Rexy and other rogue dinosaurs
recaptured on Isla Nublar.

00:13:40.529 --> 00:13:44.139
They are shipped to Site B until their enclosures
in the new park are finished.

00:13:44.139 --> 00:13:48.920
In 2003, InGen bribes members of the U.S.
House Committee of Science, who then agree

00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:53.480
to remove the restrictions on InGen because
of the Gene Guard Act, which allows them to

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:58.320
begin cloning and genetically engineering
new species of dinosaurs for Jurassic World.

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:03.626
The following year, Simon Masrani hires Claire
Dearing as an intern on the Jurassic World project.

00:14:03.626 --> 00:14:08.690
Masrani Global Corporation soon begins moving
the dinosaurs back from Site B to the new

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:13.529
park on Site A. At the time, Masrani's company
is credited with saving the creatures from

00:14:13.529 --> 00:14:14.810
ecological disaster.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:20.610
It's later revealed in 2015 that the strain
on the Isla Sorna ecosystem had actually been

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:27.590
caused by InGen's secret experiments on Isla
Sorna in 1998 when Masrani acquired the company.

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:33.465
In 2005, Simon Masrani's company opens its
new dinosaur park, Jurassic World, to the public.

00:14:33.465 --> 00:14:38.139
Elsewhere, just a few short years later, Sir
Benjamin Lockwood's daughter, Charlotte, has

00:14:38.139 --> 00:14:39.550
succeeded in cloning herself.

00:14:39.550 --> 00:14:42.029
Her daughter, Maisie, is born.

00:14:42.029 --> 00:14:46.680
While Charlotte suffers from a rare genetic
disease that leads to her death in 2009, Claire

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:49.220
continues rising through the ranks of InGen.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:52.830
She eventually becomes the senior assets manager
at Jurassic World.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:57.870
"We've learned more from genetics in the past
decade than a century of digging up bones."

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:03.740
Work on the Indominus rex begins in 2012 after
demands from Jurassic World's board of investors

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:08.459
cause Claire and Masrani to ask Dr. Henry
Wu to create a hybrid theropod.

00:15:08.459 --> 00:15:13.070
Developments in dinosaur behavior at Jurassic
World continue, with Owen Grady selected to

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:16.300
head up a special project as its head velociraptor
trainer.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:18.299
"Delta, I see you.

00:15:18.299 --> 00:15:19.107
Back up."

00:15:20.798 --> 00:15:26.529
During this time, Masrani authorizes the construction
of a new facility in Siberia in 2012, which

00:15:26.529 --> 00:15:28.639
opens in 2014.

00:15:28.639 --> 00:15:31.990
Its focus is to extract the DNA of animals
from the Ice Age.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:38.260
On Isla Nublar in 2012, a new pack of velociraptors
is engineered by Wu's team, and the raptors

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:41.490
Blue, Charlie, Delta, and Echo are born.

00:15:41.490 --> 00:15:46.839
In 2013, Owen recognizes some nuances in the
dynamic of their pack and requests that his

00:15:46.839 --> 00:15:49.209
friend Barry Sembène join his team.

00:15:49.209 --> 00:15:53.503
By 2015, Jurassic World has operated for 10
years without incident.

00:15:53.776 --> 00:15:58.130
In 2015, Simon Masrani publicly announces
that Jurassic World will soon be unveiling

00:15:58.130 --> 00:16:01.949
a new genetically engineered dinosaur: the
Indominus rex.

00:16:01.949 --> 00:16:04.725
"It tried to break the glass."

00:16:04.725 --> 00:16:05.846
"I like her spirit."

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:09.170
As a result, ticket sales rise astronomically.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:13.790
Meanwhile, Claire Dearing's nephews, Zach
and Gray Mitchell, come to visit her on Isla

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:16.600
Nublar while their parents go through divorce
proceedings.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:20.089
Their arrival coincides with Jurassic World's
first big disaster.

00:16:20.089 --> 00:16:23.910
The Indominus rex, which ate its twin when
it was younger, is much smarter than InGen

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:30.000
scientists expected and displays traits that
even Dr. Henry Wu, its creator, is surprised by.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.320
Its camouflage abilities, along with its significant
intelligence, allow it to escape.

00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:39.230
In its ensuing rampage, it nearly kills Owen,
and its carnage throughout the park causes

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:43.370
mass chaos, destruction, and further dinosaur
escapes.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:47.389
Claire and Owen team up to search for Zach
and Gray, who briefly encounter the indominus

00:16:47.389 --> 00:16:49.190
on their Gyrosphere ride.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:53.889
Meanwhile, the pteranodons escape their enclosure
when Masrani's helicopter sends the Indominus

00:16:53.889 --> 00:16:55.290
rex into the paddock.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:17:00.110
He dies when pteranodons and dimorphodons
fly into the helicopter and it crashes.

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:04.260
Then, realizing that extreme measures need
to be taken, Owen uses Blue's pack to hunt

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:05.260
the indominus.

00:17:05.260 --> 00:17:08.220
"Your boyfriend's a badass."

00:17:08.220 --> 00:17:13.230
To his and the others' dismay, they initially
side with her, sensing her velociraptor DNA.

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:17.650
However, Owen eventually gets through to Blue,
and she helps them fight the indominus.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:22.906
With the help of Rexy and a surprise assist
from the mosasaurus, the group defeats the Indominus.

00:17:22.906 --> 00:17:27.650
Despite a lot of deaths, all's well that ends
well; Zach and Grey's parents return to get

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:32.059
them together, seemingly no longer getting
divorced, while Claire and Owen walk off into

00:17:32.059 --> 00:17:33.059
the sunset.

00:17:33.059 --> 00:17:37.890
Season 1 of "Jurassic World: Camp Cretaceous"
takes place simultaneously to the events of

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:42.059
"Jurassic World," beginning just before Jack
and Gray arrive on Isla Nublar.

00:17:42.059 --> 00:17:48.000
A group of six kids — Darius, Ben, Yaz,
Brooklynn, Kenji, and Sammy — arrive on

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.090
the island to attend adventure camp.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:54.620
However, they discover problems within the
park and end up having several close encounters

00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.750
with dinosaurs like the carnotaurus.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:18:01.770
However, before their many near-death experiences,
Claire Dearing actually planned for her nephews

00:18:01.770 --> 00:18:06.786
to attend this camp, but their counselor Roxie
suggests that it would be too much to take on.

00:18:06.786 --> 00:18:11.830
As Season 1 progresses, the campers are attacked
by the Indominus rex and the mosasaurus, which

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:16.169
makes them miss the ferry off Isla Nublar,
leaving them stranded on the island.

00:18:16.169 --> 00:18:20.840
Season 2 picks up after the events of "Jurassic
World," with the island now all but abandoned.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:25.169
While trying to avoid getting killed by dinosaurs,
the kids face off against new characters Mitch

00:18:25.169 --> 00:18:30.640
and Tiff, who have come to the island claiming
to be eco-tourists, but instead are hunters

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:33.150
looking to bag some dinosaur trophies.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:37.539
Of course, they both get what's coming to
them, with Rexy taking a bite out of Mitch

00:18:37.539 --> 00:18:41.513
and Tiff being killed by the baryonyx duo
"Chaos" and "Limbo."

00:18:41.816 --> 00:18:46.110
"Jurassic World: Camp Cretaceous" Season 3
lines up with the opening scene of "Jurassic

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:50.530
World: Fallen Kingdom," which is set six months
after the events of "Jurassic World."

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:55.030
Dr. Henry Wu has just started working for
Sir Benjamin Lockwood's estate manager, Eli

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:59.590
Mills, and they've sent a group of mercenaries
to recover the bones of Indominus rex.

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:04.020
The animated series recreates pieces of this
opening scene before depicting what else was

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:05.650
going on around the island.

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:09.530
It notably reveals that Wu engineered two
types of hybrid dinosaurs.

00:19:09.530 --> 00:19:15.320
He created the Scorpios rex before the Indominus,
but Simon Masrani ordered Wu to have her killed

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:17.720
because she was too terrifying for the park.

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:22.650
However, he didn't do this, instead placing
the dinosaur into a cryofreeze chamber and

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:25.250
planning to use her to create his next hybrid.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:30.230
She is accidentally freed at the end of Season
2, and after asexually procreating between

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:34.740
the second and third seasons, she and her
child attack the campers several times.

00:19:34.740 --> 00:19:38.669
They face off against the campers for the
last time in the old Jurassic Park Visitors

00:19:38.669 --> 00:19:43.500
Center in the episode "Escape from Isla Nublar,"
where the dinosaurs are killed when the roof

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:44.500
caves in.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:48.809
Afterward, in Season 4, the campers finally
escape from Isla Nublar.

00:19:48.809 --> 00:19:53.670
Back on the mainland, Wu receives the Indominus
rex DNA the mercenaries recovered from Isla

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:57.540
Nublar and engineers a new dinosaur called
the Indoraptor.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:02.290
The following year, Claire Dearing founds
the Dinosaur Protection Group after Isla Nublar's

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:07.095
volcano Mount Sibo becomes active and threatens
to kill all the dinosaurs.

00:20:07.458 --> 00:20:12.740
In June 2018, Claire Dearing is summoned to
Sir Benjamin Lockwood's estate, where he introduces

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:15.080
himself as an old associate of John Hammond's.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:19.900
He offers to fund her rescue mission to Isla
Nublar so that she can save the dinosaurs

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:22.790
from extinction as Mount Sibo is now erupting.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:27.420
However, he requests that her now ex-boyfriend
Owen Grady also join the mission, as he's

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:29.309
the only one who can save Blue.

00:20:29.309 --> 00:20:31.190
"Back for more, huh?"

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.870
"Can I buy you a beer?"

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:36.370
"Did you bring em or do we gotta like go somewhere?"

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:41.549
Claire and Owen return to the island along
with paleoveterinarian Zia Rodriquez and IT

00:20:41.549 --> 00:20:42.830
expert Franklin Webb.

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:47.370
To their surprise, they are met by mercenary
and trophy hunter Ken Wheatley, who double-crosses

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:49.299
them and captures Blue.

00:20:49.299 --> 00:20:54.450
After a few close encounters with dinosaurs
and a near-drowning, Claire, Owen, Zia, and

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:59.010
Franklin escape the island and stow away onboard
one of Wheatley's ships, where they are taken

00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:01.020
back to the Lockwood estate.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:05.750
Benjamin has just died at the hands of Eli
Mills — who has subsequently taken control,

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:09.919
locking Lockwood's granddaughter Maisie in
her room and going ahead with his plans to

00:21:09.919 --> 00:21:12.320
bankroll further genetic research.

00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:16.770
Claire and Owen discover that Dr. Wu has created
a new hybrid called the Indoraptor.

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:20.590
Furthermore, Mills is auctioning off dinosaurs
to the highest bidder.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:25.590
But in typical Jurassic fashion, this deadly
dinosaur doesn't remain in its cage for long

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:28.120
and kills several of the guests before attacking
Maisie.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:32.830
With a little help from Blue, Claire, Owen,
and Maisie eventually trick the Indoraptor

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:36.020
so it falls through the glass roof and impales
itself.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:37.860
Mills is killed in the chaos at the mansion.

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:42.730
But when the group is faced with gas potentially
killing all the dinosaurs within the mansion,

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:45.170
Maisie makes the choice to let them all go
free.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:46.760
"I had to.

00:21:47.545 --> 00:21:51.017
They're alive like me."

00:21:51.017 --> 00:21:55.640
One year after "Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom,"
dinosaurs have spread across North America

00:21:55.640 --> 00:22:00.039
and humans begin to encounter them more and
more — and it's not long before they spread

00:22:00.039 --> 00:22:01.549
across the entire world.

00:22:01.549 --> 00:22:05.620
This is shown in the short film "Battle at
Big Rock," which gives viewers an insight

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:07.700
into what this new world looks like.

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:11.870
Centered around one family of campers at Big
Rock National Park, it begins when a mother

00:22:11.870 --> 00:22:15.020
and baby nasutoceratops wanders around their
campfire.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:19.820
The human family joins the nasutoceratops
mother and her mate in the fight against the

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:24.549
allosaurus, and it eventually leaves when
the young daughter shoots it with a crossbow.

00:22:24.549 --> 00:22:29.290
The film depicts just one of the many encounters
humans now have with dinosaurs and is a precursor

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:31.559
to what comes in "Jurassic World: Dominion."

00:22:31.559 --> 00:22:35.820
But before the epic finale can take place,
the "Jurassic Park" timeline jumps over to

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:38.070
the campers on Mantah Corp Island.

00:22:38.070 --> 00:22:42.910
Season 5 of "Jurassic Park: Camp Cretaceous"
leads directly into the third "Jurassic World"

00:22:42.910 --> 00:22:46.080
film, re-establishing Lewis Dodgson's character.

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:50.299
Voiced by Adam Harrington in the animated
series and played by Campbell Scott in "Dominion,"

00:22:50.299 --> 00:22:54.260
the CEO of BioSyn is the main antagonist for
the remainder of the franchise.

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:58.430
Although the campers foil his attempt to use
mind control chips on all the dinosaurs on

00:22:58.430 --> 00:23:02.520
the island, he gets away with the technology,
which will soon come into play.

00:23:02.796 --> 00:23:07.650
Ellie Sattler and Alan Grant reunite in "Jurassic
World: Dominion" as Lewis Dodgson invites

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:11.559
them to tour his BioSyn facility, where Ian
Malcolm now works.

00:23:11.559 --> 00:23:16.120
With help from Ian and Ramsay Cole, they quickly
discover that Dodgson and Henry Wu have been

00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:20.890
genetically engineering a swarm of prehistoric
giant locusts to destroy all crops except

00:23:20.890 --> 00:23:23.130
the ones grown with BioSyn seeds.

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:28.840
However, Wu needs Maisie Lockwood's DNA to
fix a genetic defect in the locusts, so Dodgson

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:33.065
has her and Blue's child, Beta, kidnapped
from the Sierra Nevada Mountains.

00:23:33.065 --> 00:23:34.404
"Claire!

00:23:35.159 --> 00:23:35.706
They found her!"

00:23:35.706 --> 00:23:36.706
"What?

00:23:36.918 --> 00:23:37.495
Who are they?"

00:23:37.495 --> 00:23:38.495
"Poachers.

00:23:38.495 --> 00:23:39.495
I've seen em around."

00:23:39.646 --> 00:23:44.200
Claire and Owen mount a rescue mission to
save them, tracking them to Malta, where they

00:23:44.200 --> 00:23:49.750
meet cargo pilot Kayla Watts, who agrees to
fly them to the BioSyn facility in the Dolomites.

00:23:49.750 --> 00:23:54.890
Inside the facility, Ellie, Alan, Ian, and
Ramsay help Maisie escape and steal a locust

00:23:54.890 --> 00:23:56.520
sample in the process.

00:23:56.520 --> 00:24:00.809
Maisie reunites with her parents and introduces
them to the "Jurassic Park" legends.

00:24:00.809 --> 00:24:01.809
"Dr. Grant?

00:24:02.050 --> 00:24:03.400
Here you are.

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:04.391
I'm Owen Grady.

00:24:04.482 --> 00:24:05.482
Big fan.

00:24:05.482 --> 00:24:06.210
I read your book.

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:08.090
Well, book on tape."

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:12.890
To destroy evidence of his attempted crimes,
Dodgson sets fire to the locusts, but the

00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:14.870
flames engulf the entire facility.

00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:18.360
He is killed by three dilophosauruses before
he can escape.

00:24:18.360 --> 00:24:22.789
However, he leaves the mind-controlled giganotosaurus
as a parting gift.

00:24:22.789 --> 00:24:27.220
Thankfully, Rexy is there to save the day
alongside a therizinosaurus, and the group

00:24:27.220 --> 00:24:30.350
then rescues Wu, who plans to stop the locusts.

00:24:30.350 --> 00:24:33.620
Claire and Owen take Maisie home and reunite
Blue with Beta.

00:24:33.620 --> 00:24:37.669
Meanwhile, Ellie and Alan get back together
and plan to go public about BioSyn.

00:24:37.669 --> 00:24:43.149
The BioSyn Valley is declared a dinosaur sanctuary
by the United Nations, leaving the world with

00:24:43.149 --> 00:24:46.570
the formidable task of coexisting with these
prehistoric animals.

